// The people of settlements: one species per calling, so a player sees who is who
// ("Baker", "Guard"). Settlements place them (settlements.ron `people`), never the land
// (kind Villager); the server keeps them only near players (crates/server/src/villagers.rs).
//
// Every person is built of the same boxes (a calling's hat and apron besides): skin by the
// climate of the land about (fairer in the cold), a shirt from their calling's colours,
// trousers, hair, and a height of their own. Colours 0 to 5 are shirt, trousers, belt and
// boots, hair, hat and apron (or a guard's iron). People of one region share a mix, so a
// village's folk look like kin. Their mind is a routine (`Routine`): where their day sends
// them, they go; struck, they run, and the guards come. Striking folk teaches nothing
// (`xp.combat` 0): only guards, who fight back, give combat experience. Their barks (a
// greeting, an alarm, a content sigh: creature_sounds.ron's voices) carry their own
// `barking` range (`greet`, `alarm`, `content`, in blocks) to players who see them, each
// bark to the same player once in `barking.every` seconds (ranges 1 to 64, every 0 to
// 600, or the content fails to load).
